  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When reading a variable in Udon, the visible execution flow does not pass through the node. All that is known is that the read occurs some time before its value is used.\nHowever, when the variable in question is set earlier in the execution flow[within the same event], it is not clear from the graph whether or not the read occurs before or after the set.\nHowever, it gets even worse when the output of the same variable read node is used both before and after the set in the graph[on the same event execution flow].\nIs the read performed again after the set(effectively splitting a variable read node into two nodes), or is the output from before the set held on the stack?\n\nMy proposed solution is adding a variable get node that does pass through the visible execution flow, to specifically define when the read occurs(the existing variable get nodes' behaviour wouldn't be changed)\n\nSee the attached images for example graph snippets where the order of reads can change results but isn't apparent from the graph.",
